# 共用提示詞片段（source 進來用）
STYLE="Pixel art sprite sheet, same art style, proportions and character design as the reference image (refined chibi pixel art, about 3 heads tall, big head, clean dark outlines, HD-2D fantasy RPG). Proportions: exactly 3 heads tall like the girl in the top strip of the reference — a big round head about one third of the total height, short torso, short legs; never a slim 4-5 head-tall body. Do not add or change any clothing, hair or accessories."
LAYOUT8="Layout: exactly 2 rows x 4 columns = 8 full-body figures of the same character, same scale, evenly spaced on a plain flat light gray background (#DDDDDD), no grid lines, no text, no ground shadows, figures and effects never touch the neighbouring figure. Read left to right, top row then bottom row = frames 1 to 8 of ONE attack animation. Frame 1 and frame 8 are the same calm ready stance. Feet of every figure on the same baseline in each row. Every hand has 5 fingers, exactly two arms, two legs."
FRONT="All 8 frames: front view facing the viewer, seen from slightly above (top-down 3/4 RPG camera), attacking toward the viewer / toward the bottom of the screen."
SIDE="All 8 frames: strict side view facing RIGHT (body, head and eyes all point to the right, profile; never look back at the viewer), attacking toward the right."
BACK="All 8 frames: back view seen from behind (face not visible, we see the back of the head), attacking away from the viewer toward the top of the screen."
DSIDE="All 8 frames: three-quarter FRONT view clearly turned 45 degrees toward the lower RIGHT corner (nose, chest and toes point to the lower right, the far shoulder partly hidden, face seen at an angle not straight on, head and body turned the same way, eyes looking down-right, not straight at the viewer), attacking toward the lower right of the screen."
USIDE="All 8 frames: three-quarter BACK view turned 45 degrees toward the upper RIGHT (we see mostly the back and the back of the head with only a sliver of the right cheek, head and body turned the same way, never looking back at the viewer), attacking toward the upper right of the screen."
